.TH LLM-BILL 1 "2026-11-01" "llm-bill 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llm-bill \- summarise LLM token usage and cost from saved API responses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
llm-bill [OPTIONS] <FILES>...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summarise LLM token usage and cost per provider, model and day from saved API
responses or the normalised JSONL. Reads files only, no network.
.PP
There are no subcommands.
A file argument of
.B -
reads standard input.
Each file must be valid UTF-8.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILES...
Input files;
.B -
reads standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print JSON instead of the text table
.TP
.B --require-cost
Exit 2 when a row has tokens but no known cost
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print help
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print version
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The summary was written to standard output.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage (unknown option, or no files), bad input, a row with tokens but no
known cost when
.B --require-cost
is set, or a failed write to standard output.
Program errors on standard error start with \fBfout:\fP.
Usage errors from the argument parser start with \fBerror:\fP.
.SH EXAMPLES
Text report of the fictional file
.IR examples/one-row.json .
Exit status 0.
.PP
.nf
llm-bill examples/one-row.json
.fi
.PP
The same file as JSON. Exit status 0.
.PP
.nf
llm-bill --json examples/one-row.json
.fi
